UPDATE companies SET description='Stuart''s Sheet Metal operates in Austin, Texas, and has served Central Texas for over 30 years. The business is family-owned and operated, though the exact founding year and founders'' names are not disclosed. It began as a sheet metal fabrication shop focused on custom metalwork for residential and commercial projects.

The shop provides custom sheet metal fabrication, including on-site and in-house roll forming for standing seam roof systems (1-inch and 1.5-inch profiles), flashing (drip edge, valley, hip), chimney caps and chase covers, drain pans for water heaters and HVAC equipment, and window and door pans. It stocks flat sheets and coils in galvanized, Galvalume, painted (Berridge and McElroy colors), bonderized, stainless steel, and 16-ounce copper, and fulfills bulk orders with a 500-linear-foot minimum.

Customers include homeowners, roofers, builders, general contractors, custom home builders, waterproofing contractors, and architects across Central Texas. Reviews cite work for roof flashings, chimney covers, custom valley collector heads, and AC drip pans.

The company emphasizes fast turnaround, precision fabrication (with one review noting 1/16-inch accuracy), and a no-middleman approach, positioning its family ownership and three-decade local experience as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom sheet metal fabrication", "On-site roll forming", "In-house roll forming", "Standing seam roof panel fabrication (1-inch, 1.5-inch)", "Snap-lock and double-lock roof systems", "Flashing fabrication (drip edge, valley, hip, custom roof/wall flashing)", "Chimney cap and chase cover fabrication", "Sheet metal drain pan fabrication", "Window and door pan fabrication", "Metal roof supply takeoffs and estimates", "Bulk material supply and delivery", "Material stocking (flat sheets and coils)"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Roofing", "Architecture", "Waterproofing", "HVAC"], "materials": ["Galvanized steel (22, 24, 26, 28 gauge)", "Galvalume (24, 26 gauge)", "Painted steel (Berridge colors, 24 gauge)", "Painted steel (McElroy colors, 24 gauge)", "Bonderized steel (24, 26 gauge)", "Stainless steel (24, 26 gauge)", "Copper (16 ounce)", "Galvalume coils", "Painted coils (Berridge colors)", "Painted coils (McElroy colors)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["30+ years serving Central Texas", "Fast turnaround on custom and stock orders", "Family owned and operated", "Custom fabrication with no middlemen", "On-site roll forming capability"], "facts_used": ["Location: Austin, Texas -> db", "Family-owned and operated -> /services", "Over 30 years experience -> /about-us, /services", "Custom sheet metal fabrication, on-site roll forming -> /services", "Standing seam roof systems (1-inch, 1.5-inch) -> /services", "Flashing fabrication (drip edge, valley, hip, custom) -> /services", "Chimney caps and chase covers -> /services", "Drain pans for water heaters and HVAC -> /services", "Window and door pans -> /services", "Materials stocked: galvanized, Galvalume, painted (Berridge, McElroy), bonderized, stainless steel, copper -> /services", "Bulk orders minimum 500 linear feet -> /services", "Customers: homeowners, roofers, builders, contractors, architects, waterproofing companies -> /, /services", "Fast turnaround claimed -> /services", "Precision fabrication noted in review (1/16 inch) -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Stuart''s Sheet Metal in Austin, can custom fabricate a wide range of products to fit your specific job requirements.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "500 linear feet for bulk orders", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='stuart-s-sheet-metal' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Studio Wise operates from Grand Rapids, Michigan, where it develops and manufactures furniture in collaboration with MatchLine Design Group. The company does not disclose its founding year or ownership structure.

The firm produces a range of tables and surfaces for dining, conference, team, and mobile settings. Its collections include Vesuvius, Stylos, Pinnacle, Pose, Zeplin, City, Strut, Apex, Geo, Blox, Parson, Staple, Elements, and Stein. Surface options feature Fuse Butcherblock, Studio Quartz, and Slatted Exterior finishes, marketed as premium materials for appearance and stability. The company emphasizes a platform for flexible, adaptive designs that deliver a custom feel at scalable volumes.

Its product categories span dining, mobile, team, and conference configurations.

The company positions itself as design-obsessed with uncompromising standards, aiming to create beautiful, purposeful pieces that help tell a better story in any space. It highlights the use of premium materials for superior appearance and stability, ensuring a unique and timeless finish.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Furniture design", "Furniture manufacturing", "Custom furniture production", "Surface finishing (butcherblock, quartz, slatted exterior)", "Flexible/adaptive design platform"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Butcherblock", "Quartz", "Slatted exterior materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Design-obsessed with uncompromising standards", "Custom feel at the scale you need", "Premium materials for superior appearance and stability", "Flexible and adaptive design platform", "Unique and timeless finish"], "facts_used": ["Location: Grand Rapids, Michigan -> /", "Develops and manufactures furniture -> /", "Designer: MatchLine Design Group -> /", "Collections: Vesuvius, Stylos, Pinnacle, Pose, Zeplin, City, Strut, Apex, Geo, Blox, Parson, Staple, Elements, Stein -> /", "Categories: Dining, Mobile, Team, Conference -> /", "Surfaces: Fuse Butcherblock, Studio Quartz, Slatted Exterior -> /", "Custom feel at scale -> /", "Design-obsessed with uncompromising standards -> /", "Premium materials for superior appearance and stability -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "we develop and manufacture beautiful, purposeful furniture in Grand Rapids, Michigan", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='studio-wise' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Stuke Iowa operates from Houghton, Iowa, where it was established in 1992 as a family-owned business. The company traces its roots to a German plastics engineering firm founded in 1967, and today operates as Ferdinand Stuekerjuergen Inc. doing business as Stuke Iowa.

The 30,000-square-foot facility produces custom plastic parts and profiles through extrusion, injection molding, and 3D printing (additive manufacturing for ABS, PC, and PEI/Ultem). Additional capabilities include assembly, in-house painting, and surface finishing, supported by milling, drilling, sanding, and polishing equipment.

Stuke Iowa serves the agriculture, construction, food, technical, and aerospace industries. The company emphasizes close customer communication and draws on engineering support from its German subsidiaries for material research and process integration.

The company states that quality and reliability are its main focus, backed by ISO 9001 and AS 9100 certifications. Partnerships with external laboratories provide specialized testing such as smoke, toxicity, heat release, environmental (DO160), fungus resistance, and shaker testing.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','AS 9100']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Extrusion", "Injection Molding", "3D Printing (Additive Manufacturing)", "Assembly", "In-house Painting", "Surface Finishing", "Packaging", "Dimensional Inspection", "First Article Inspection (AS9102)", "Production Monitoring", "Material Research (with German subsidiaries)", "Process Integration (with German subsidiaries)", "Burn Testing (CS/FAR 25.853)", "Color Measurement", "Roughness Measurement", "Moisture Testing", "Paint Adhesion Testing", "3D Measuring", "Smoke/Toxicity/Heat Release Testing", "Environmental Testing (DO160)", "Fungus Resistance Testing", "Shaker Testing"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Construction", "Food", "Technical", "Aerospace"], "materials": ["ABS", "HDPO", "HIPS", "PA", "PC", "PE", "PEI (Ultem)", "PES", "PP", "PVC", "TPE", "TPV"], "equipment": ["Milling machines", "Drilling machines", "Sanding machines", "Polishing machines", "3D printers (ABS, PC, PEI/Ultem)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned with 50+ years of German plastics engineering heritage", "ISO 9001 and AS 9100 certified quality management", "In-house painting, assembly, and surface finishing under one roof", "Engineering collaboration with German subsidiaries for material research and process integration", "External laboratory partnerships for aerospace-grade testing (smoke, toxicity, environmental, fungus, shaker)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1992 as family-owned business -> /about", "German parent company founded 1967 -> /about", "Facility approx. 30,000 sq ft -> /about", "Processes: extrusion, injection molding, 3D printing, assembly, in-house painting -> /about", "Materials: ABS, HDPO, HIPS, PA, PC, PE, PEI (Ultem), PES, PP, PVC, TPE, TPV -> /", "Industries: agriculture, construction, food, technical, aerospace -> /about", "Certifications: ISO 9001, AS 9100 -> /quality", "Quality tests: burn test (CS/FAR 25.853), color measurement, roughness, moisture, paint adhesion, 3D measuring, smoke/toxicity/heat release, environmental (DO160), fungus resistance, shaker -> /quality", "General Manager: Frank Stuekerjuergen -> /about", "Company legal name: Ferdinand Stuekerjuergen Inc. dba. STUKE IOWA -> /about", "Headquarters: Houghton, Iowa 52631, 1498 Highway 16 -> /about", "Engineering support from German subsidiaries -> /about", "External laboratory partnerships -> /quality"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "HIGH-QUALITY CUSTOMIZED PLASTIC PARTS MANUFACTURING", "founded_year": "1992", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='stuke-iowa' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sumitomo Chemical Advanced Technologies, a wholly owned subsidiary of Japan’s Sumitomo Chemical Co., Ltd., operates from a 50,000-square-foot facility in Phoenix, Arizona. The U.S. entity was formed in 2003 when Sumitomo Chemical acquired the assets of ATMI’s GaAs epitaxial wafer business, building on epitaxial research that dates back to 1971.

The company develops and manufactures compound-semiconductor epitaxial wafers using metalorganic chemical vapor deposition (MOCVD) on 2‑ to 6‑inch substrates, running eleven Aixtron reactors (2600 G3, 2400/2600 G3, and 2800 G4 models) with a stated capacity exceeding 100,000 wafers per year. It also produces super engineering plastics such as LCP, PES, and PPSU under the Sumikasuper and Sumikaexcel brands, compounds Penacolite resins for tire and rubber applications, grinds PES for advanced composites, and formulates photoresists, wet chemicals, polarizing films, and lithium‑battery separators.

Customers span the semiconductor, wireless, automotive, consumer-electronics, solar-energy, medical-device, tire-and-rubber, and composite-materials sectors. The epitaxial foundry supplies HBT, pHEMT, LED, diode, and VCSEL wafers for wireless and optical communications, while engineering plastics and resins serve automotive connectors, industrial components, and medical applications. Photoresist and optical-film products target semiconductor lithography and display manufacturers.

The business was created to strengthen Sumitomo Chemical’s position in the global semiconductor and IT-related materials market, leveraging the parent’s century-old commitment to solving environmental problems through chemistry. The company emphasizes a “Culture of Customer Focus” with goals of zero returns, 100% on-time delivery, and 100% customer satisfaction, backed by ISO 9001, ISO 14001, IATF 16949, and ISO 45001 certifications.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 14001:2015','IATF 16949:2016','ISO 45001:2018','RoHS compliant','REACH compliant','Dodd-Frank Conflict Minerals Regulation compliant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["MOCVD epitaxial wafer manufacturing", "Super engineering plastics manufacturing (LCP, PES, PPSU)", "Penacolite compounding resins production", "PES grinding for advanced composites", "High purity alumina production", "Photoresist and wet chemicals development", "Polarizing film development and supply", "Lithium battery separator development", "Resorcinol resins production", "Rubber chemicals production", "Polymer additives production", "Semiconductor process materials development", "Optical films development", "Epitaxial wafer foundry services (HBT, pHEMT, LED, diode, VCSEL)", "Engineering plastics specification and sales", "Resin grinding", "Super engineering plastics sales (Sumiploy, IGETABOND)", "Photoresist resins and chemicals sales", "Epitaxial wafer sales", "Polarizing film sales"], "industries": ["Semiconductor", "Wireless communications", "Automotive", "Consumer electronics", "Solar energy", "Medical devices", "Tire and rubber goods", "Composite materials", "Display manufacturing", "Lithium battery", "Industrial applications", "Agriculture", "Pharmaceutical", "Personal care", "Wood adhesive", "Dyes", "UVA"], "materials": ["Gallium Arsenide (GaAs)", "Gallium Nitride (GaN)", "Indium Gallium Phosphide (InGaP)", "Aluminum Gallium Arsenide (AlGaAs)", "Liquid Crystal Polymer (LCP)", "Polyethersulfone (PES)", "Polyphenylsulfone (PPSU)", "Epoxy resins", "High Purity Alumina (HPA)", "Resorcinol", "Penacolite resins", "Photoresist chemicals", "Polarizing film materials", "Lithium battery membrane materials", "Rubber chemicals", "Polymer additives"], "equipment": ["6 Aixtron 2600 G3 systems (5x150mm or 8x100mm)", "1 Aixtron 2400/2600 G3 system (5x100mm)", "4 Aixtron 2800 G4 systems (8x150mm)", "Veeco E450 reactor", "Full characterization facilities including large area device fab"], "volume": "Capacity >100,000 wafers/year", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["24/7 engineering support in a completely tooled facility", "Capacity exceeding 100,000 wafers per year", "Full in-house characterization and large-area device fabrication", "Facility expandable to 19 MOCVD reactors", "ISO 9001, ISO 14001, IATF 16949, and ISO 45001 certified"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Phoenix, Arizona -> /about-us", "Founded as US subsidiary in 2003 via ATMI asset acquisition -> /about-us", "Wholly owned subsidiary of Sumitomo Chemical Co., Ltd. -> /about-us", "50,000 sq. ft. total facility, 30,000 sq. ft. manufacturing, 6,000 sq. ft. clean room -> /about-us", "Eleven Aixtron reactors (models listed) with capacity >100,000 wafers/year -> /about-us", "Manufactures epitaxial wafers (HBT, pHEMT, LED, diode, VCSEL) via MOCVD -> /", "Produces super engineering plastics (LCP, PES, PPSU) under Sumikasuper/Sumikaexcel brands -> /", "Compounds Penacolite resins for tire/rubber industries -> /", "PES grinding for advanced composites -> /", "Develops photoresists, wet chemicals, polarizing films, lithium battery separators -> /", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, ISO 14001:2015, IATF 16949:2016, ISO 45001:2018, RoHS, REACH, Conflict Minerals -> /about-us", "Serves semiconductor, wireless, automotive, consumer electronics, solar, medical, tire/rubber, composites -> /about-us, /", "24/7 engineering support, full characterization, device fab -> /about-us", "Facility expandable to 19 reactors -> /about-us", "Parent company Sumitomo Chemical founded 1913 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Sumitomo Chemical Advanced Technologies manufactures custom epitaxial wafers using MOCVD (Metalorganic Chemical Vapor Deposition) in our state-of-the-art facility in Phoenix, AZ.", "founded_year": "2003", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["NAFTA region distribution"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sumitomo-chemical-advanced-technologies-dba-sumika-electronic-materials' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Summit Plastic Molding was founded in 1982 in Shelby Township, Michigan, opening its doors as a tool shop before expanding into a full-service injection molding supplier. The company operates four facilities across Michigan, Texas, and China, with its headquarters remaining in Shelby Township.

The company provides custom injection molding from 85 to 1,000 tons, combining in-house tool building, tool maintenance, and production molding under one roof. A joint venture in Shenzhen, China, established in 2002, adds low-cost tooling capacity.

Summit serves the automotive, medical, and defense sectors, delivering both prototype and production-volume parts.

The company emphasizes a one-stop, fully integrated model that spans engineering, tooling, and manufacturing, aiming to reduce lead times and logistics costs through its global footprint. Leadership cites total customer service and quality focus as drivers for its growth from a tool shop to a multi-site molder.', certifications=ARRAY['IATF 16949','ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding (85\u20131,000 ton)", "Tool building", "Tool maintenance", "CNC machining (HAAS, Makino)", "Prototyping", "Production molding", "Mold making"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Medical", "Defense"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Engel 560-ton injection molding machine", "HAAS CNC machine", "Makino Carbon Cutter CNC", "Makino CNC"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One-stop full-service injection molding supplier with in-house engineering, tooling, and manufacturing", "In-house tool building, maintenance, and production molding across all facilities", "Global footprint with facilities in Michigan, Texas, and China for logistics savings", "IATF 16949 and ISO 9001 certified quality systems", "Injection molding capacity from 85 to 1,000 tons"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1982 in Shelby Township, Michigan -> db", "Headquarters: Shelby Township, Michigan -> db", "Certifications: IATF 16949, ISO 9001 -> db", "Capabilities: Custom injection molding 85-1000 ton, in-house tool building, maintenance, production molding -> db", "Facilities: Michigan (manufacturing facility and tool shop), Texas (125,000 sq ft since 1990), China joint venture since 2002 -> /", "Industries served: automotive, medical, defense -> /", "Equipment: Engel 560-ton injection molding machine, HAAS CNC, Makino Carbon Cutter CNC, Makino CNC -> /", "Company began as tool shop in 1982, expanded to full-service -> /", "Tool shop opened 2020 in Michigan -> /", "One-stop full-service supplier claim -> /", "IATF 16949 certified at Texas facility -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Summit Plastic Molding specializes in prototyping and production injection molding for the automotive, medical, and defense sectors.", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='summit-plastic-molding' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sun State Plastics began in 1972 in North Canton, Ohio.

The operation runs 22 injection molding machines with clamping forces from 28 to 1,100 tons, supported by four material silos that hold up to 380,000 pounds of resin. The plant includes three shipping docks and two ground-level doors, and offers custom injection molding, thermoplastic injection molding, assembly, packaging, and warehousing services under one roof.

The company serves customers needing custom molded plastic parts, assembly, and storage, though specific industry sectors are not listed in its public materials.

