UPDATE companies SET description='Superior Machine & Welding operates from Anchorage, Alaska, where it has occupied a site on Ship Avenue since 1950. The business began when Jack L. Whitmore purchased a 3,400-square-foot shop and later reclaimed adjacent land from Ship Creek to expand. A 1964 addition brought the facility to 10,000 square feet, adding two Lodge & Shipley oil-country lathes and a five-ton overhead crane. Today the company is owned by WOSB-certified Jantina Lunsford, Whitmore''s daughter, continuing the family-owned legacy.

The shop provides full-service machining, welding, and custom fabrication for repair and new-build work. Welding covers TIG, MIG, stick, and brazing in materials from mild steel and aluminum to exotic alloys such as Inconel, Hastelloy, and titanium. The facility also houses 40- and 160-ton hydraulic presses, horizontal and vertical band saws, and a 3D CNC programming station.

Customers span Alaska''s marine, heavy-equipment, oilfield, construction, and government sectors. The shop regularly repairs cast-iron components, rebuilds shafts and bores to OEM specifications for marine and heavy-equipment applications, and machines oilfield directional-drill timing rings. Clients range from federal and state agencies to corporations and private individuals.

The company emphasizes that its local presence eliminates the long lead times and high freight costs of sourcing from the lower 48. It backs every job with a guarantee against workmanship defects and highlights its multi-generational machinist experience—over 100 combined years—as a differentiator for tackling complex geometries and difficult materials that other shops decline.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Large-bore turning (Lodge & Shipley oil-country lathes)", "Thread chasing (API, NPT, ACME, buttress, etc.) ID/OD", "Horizontal boring (5-axis manual, 3-axis CNC)", "Vertical knee milling (with rotary table, 90\u00b0 head, dividing head)", "Gear cutting (spur gears, OD splines)", "Blanchard grinding (\u00b10.00038 in)", "Tool post grinding (centerless between centers)", "Vertical shaping (internal keyways, splines up to 4 ft diameter)", "CNC turning (2-axis toolroom lathe, high repeatability)", "CNC milling (custom 4-axis Bridgeport conversion)", "CNC plasma/oxy-fuel cutting (4x8 ft, 18 ga to 1 in mild steel)", "Hydraulic pressing (40-ton and 160-ton)", "Horizontal band sawing (18 in, up to 48 in feed, \u00b10.010 in repeatability)", "Vertical band sawing (scrolling, small jobs)", "3D CNC programming (complex geometries, cycle-time optimization)", "TIG welding (Lincoln, Miller)", "MIG welding (Miller CPU-controlled with steel/aluminum wire feeders)", "Stick welding (Miller buzz boxes)", "Brazing (special brass alloys up to 100,000 PSI, 1200\u00b0F)", "Cast iron repair welding", "Shaft/bore buildup and re-machining to OE specs", "Exotic alloy welding (Inconel, Hastelloy, Stellite, titanium, etc.)"], "industries": ["Marine", "Heavy equipment", "Oil and gas", "Construction", "Government / military", "State agencies", "Commercial/industrial", "Private/residential"], "materials": ["Mild steel", "Alloy steel", "T1 steel", "Chromoly", "Stainless steel (all grades, including 17-4PH)", "Cast iron", "Cast steel", "Aluminum", "Silicon bronze",