UPDATE companies SET description='Sustar Woodworks was founded in 2012 by Ian Sustar in Milwaukee, Wisconsin. Raised in his father’s woodworking shop, Sustar developed an early appreciation for the craft before studying engineering and eventually returning to furniture making. The company operates from a Milwaukee workshop where each piece is designed and built.

The shop produces built-to-order furniture using North American hardwoods and time-honored joinery techniques. Every item is made individually, emphasizing construction methods chosen for integrity and longevity rather than nostalgia. The work blends Shaker utility with mid-century modern influence, resulting in pieces that feel familiar without belonging to a specific period.

The company invites inquiries for projects that align with its design language, which prioritizes thoughtful proportion, honest materials, and purposeful details.

The founder’s philosophy echoes a Shaker principle: don’t make something unless it is both necessary and useful, but if it is, don’t hesitate to make it beautiful. This ethos drives a focus on furniture meant to be used, lived with, and kept for generations.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Handcrafted woodworking", "Joinery", "Furniture construction", "Built-to-order manufacturing"], "industries": ["Furniture", "Woodworking", "Custom furniture"], "materials": ["Hardwoods", "North American hardwoods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Built-to-order from premium North American hardwoods", "Time-honored joinery and construction techniques", "Each piece made individually for integrity and long life", "Design grounded in Shaker and mid-century modern principles", "Furniture meant to be used, lived with, and kept"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2012 by Ian Sustar in Milwaukee, Wisconsin -> /about", "Raised in father''s woodworking shop, studied engineering -> /about", "Operates from Milwaukee workshop -> /about", "Produces built-to-order furniture from North American hardwoods -> /", "Uses time-honored joinery and construction techniques -> /about", "Each piece made individually -> /about", "Design blends Shaker utility with mid-century modern influence -> /", "Serves clients seeking custom furniture commissions -> /", "Philosophy: thoughtful proportion, honest materials, purposeful details -> /about", "Shaker quote about necessary, useful, beautiful -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Each piece is built-to-order from premium hardwoods.", "founded_year": "2012", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sustar-woodworks' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Swirl Woodcraft was founded in 1990 in Salt Lake City, Utah. The company operates as a custom cabinetry and fine woodworking studio serving residential, commercial, and hospitality clients across the Intermountain West and nationwide.

The 40,000-square-foot production facility houses CNC routers, digital measuring tools, and CAD software that integrate with a team of designers, engineers, and skilled artisans. A 5,000-square-foot showroom displays material samples and finished examples. The company manages every phase in-house—from design and engineering through fabrication, finishing, and installation—allowing it to handle complex, large-scale luxury projects while maintaining boutique-level attention to detail.

Swirl Woodcraft’s portfolio spans high-end private residences, luxury vacation homes, boutique hotels, commercial offices, and resort properties. Its client base includes homeowners, contractors, interior designers, and property developers. Woods such as knotty alder, rustic cherry, rustic walnut, sand-blasted pine, clear alder, walnut, white oak, maple, and cherry are offered across traditional, modern, and rustic style lines for kitchens, baths, and architectural millwork.

