UPDATE companies SET description='TW Garner Food Company traces its roots to 1929 in Winston-Salem, North Carolina, when the Garner family created a barbecue sauce that gained local acclaim during the Great Depression. The family-owned business began with that single sauce and expanded into a broader line of condiments.

Today the company manufactures a range of hot sauces and salsas under the Texas Pete and Green Mountain Gringo brands. Its portfolio includes the original Texas Pete Hot Sauce, ¡Sabor! by Texas Pete Mexican-Style Hot Sauce, CHA! by Texas Pete Sriracha Sauce, and Green Mountain Gringo Salsa.

The company serves the foodservice industry through its Texas Pete Foodservice line and the retail grocery market via Texas Pete Retail and Green Mountain Gringo.

