UPDATE companies SET description='Tailored Industry operates from Industry City in Brooklyn, New York. The company was founded by Alex Tschopp, who serves as co‑founder and CEO, after he experienced the difficulties of small‑scale manufacturing while running a collegiate wholesale business. Frustrated by high minimums and the scarcity of domestic knitting mills, he began producing sweaters in‑house and later pivoted to an on‑demand model when brands of all sizes asked for low‑quantity, quick‑turnaround knitwear.

The factory specializes in on‑demand knitwear using 3D knitting technology and automated equipment, complemented by skilled finishing and quality‑control teams. Starting with four machines in a 500‑square‑foot space at the Brooklyn Army Terminal, the operation has expanded its machine count and now offers a library of over 300 market‑ready styles. Production is zero‑waste — no cutting or sewing — and orders can launch in as few as nine business days. The facility also provides yarn‑stock service and embroidery.

Tailored Industry serves fashion brands, apparel companies, and e‑commerce merchants seeking custom knitwear and merchandise. Customers include Porsche Brooklyn for branded merchandise, Oliver Charles for bootstrapped fashion lines, Tigerbob for artistic knits, and Ministry of Supply for built‑to‑order production. The platform integrates directly with Shopify for real‑time order tracking and drop shipping.

The company was created to give brands what they want, when they want it: no minimums, full transparency, and domestic production that blends heritage craftsmanship with advanced software. Its founders aimed to eliminate the inventory risk and hidden costs that plague traditional manufacturing, offering a sustainable, flexible alternative for brands of any size.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["On-demand knitwear manufacturing", "3D knitting", "Automated knitting equipment operation", "Finishing and quality control", "Custom knitwear development", "Ready-to-sell style library (STK)", "Shopify integration for production tracking", "Drop shipping", "Zero-waste production (no cutting, no sewing)", "Small batch production", "Silhouette and fit customization", "Custom development (Flagship tier)", "Yarn-stock service", "Embroidery", "Real-time production visibility"], "industries": ["Fashion brands", "Apparel companies", "Custom merchandise", "Knitwear manufacturing", "E-commerce brands"], "materials": ["Eco-Viscose", "Cotton", "Merino", "Cashmere", "Sorona"], "equipment": ["3D knitting machines", "Automated knitting equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "9 business days for on-demand production", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Zero minimum order quantities", "Order-to-launch in 9 business days", "300+ ready-to-sell styles in STK library", "Seamless Shopify integration for real-time production tracking", "Zero-waste 3D knitting (no cutting, no sewing)"], "facts_used": ["Founded by Alex Tschopp after challenges in small-scale manufacturing -> /about", "Located in Industry City, Brooklyn, New York -> /about", "Started with 4 machines in 500 sq ft at Brooklyn Army Terminal -> /about", "Uses 3D knitting technology and automated equipment -> /about", "Zero-waste production (no cutting, no sewing) -> /about", "Offers 300+ market-ready styles in STK library -> /", "Order to launch in 9 business days -> /", "No minimum order quantities -> /", "Shopify integration for real-time tracking -> /", "Serves brands like Porsche Brooklyn, Oliver Charles, Tigerbob, Ministry of Supply -> /", "Materials: Eco-Viscose, Cotton, Merino, Cashmere, Sorona -> /", "Collective team experience of 100+ years in knitwear -> /about", "Yarn-stock service and embroidery available -> /", "Three membership tiers: Boutique, Studio, Flagship -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our factory in Industry City combines a harmonious blend of skill and expertise. We employ individuals with garment manufacturing expertise, who have worked in knitting factories, apparel factories, as fashion designers, machine programmers, electricians, entrepreneurs, and the list goes on.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "No minimum order quantity", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/tailored-industry/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tailored-industry-factory' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Taiyo America Inc. operates from Carson City, Nevada, where it was established in 1990 as a manufacturing subsidiary of Japan''s Taiyo Holdings Co., Ltd. (founded 1953). The company began by supplying solder mask products, legend inks, thermal management inks, and direct imaging materials to the printed circuit board industry.

Today Taiyo America produces a broad line of liquid and dry-film solder masks—including the PSR-4000 family—legend inks, hole-plugging and gap-filling compounds, dielectric and conductive inks, and inkjet-printable solder masks. Its materials are applied via screen printing, spray, curtain coating, and inkjet processes. The firm also designs and manufactures PCB coating and drying equipment under the Taiyo Circuit Automation brand. Regional sales, engineering, and service teams support customers across North America and Europe.

The company serves aerospace and defense, medical, automotive, and consumer electronics markets. Its materials have been used on the F-35 fighter jet, the Mars MER-1 rover, the X-59 Quesst X-plane, and satellites; in hearing aids, blood-pressure monitors, and imaging equipment; in electric vehicles, brake systems, and LED lighting; and in smartphones, smart watches, laptops, and tablets.

Taiyo America emphasizes heavy R&D investment to deliver innovations such as high-resolution FLEXFINER dry film and advanced inkjet solder masks. It cites a proven track record, service from experienced regional teams, and a customer-retention philosophy that treats clients “like family” as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['UL LISTED','ROHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solder mask formulation and manufacturing (liquid and dry film)", "Legend ink formulation (inkjet, screen, spray)", "Thermal management ink development", "Direct imaging materials", "Hole plugging and gap filling compounds", "Dielectric and conductive ink formulation for printed electronics", "Inkjet-printable solder mask technology", "Screen printing, spray coating, curtain coating application support", "PCB coating and drying equipment design and manufacturing (Taiyo Circuit Automation)", "Technical support and process engineering for PCB fabrication"], "industries": ["Aerospace and Defense", "Medical", "Automotive", "Consumer Electronics", "Printed Electronics", "Lighting and Display"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Taiyo Circuit Automation PCB coating and drying equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Ships by end of next business day for in-stock products", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Global market leader in specialty inks and solder masks for PCBs", "Heavy R&D investment yielding innovations like FLEXFINER dry film and inkjet solder masks", "Regional sales, engineering, and service teams across North America and Europe", "PSR-4000 solder mask family approved for mission-critical aerospace applications", "In-house design and manufacture of PCB coating and drying equipment (Taiyo Circuit Automation)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1990 -> db, /about-us", "Headquarters Carson City, Nevada -> db", "Subsidiary of Taiyo Holdings Co., Ltd. (Japan, founded 1953) -> /about-us", "Products: solder masks, legend inks, thermal management inks, direct imaging, dry film, inkjet solder ma