UPDATE companies SET description='Tasly Pharmaceuticals, Inc. was founded in 2006 and is headquartered in Rockville, Maryland. The company was established to integrate botanical science with modern pharmaceutical innovation, developing safe, effective, and scientifically validated botanical medicines that complement conventional treatments.

The company develops and manufactures botanical drugs, most notably T89 (Dantonic), the first herbal medicine-derived compound to complete an FDA Phase III global clinical trial. Production runs on what Tasly describes as the world''s largest proprietary automatic dripping pill and packaging line, a fully automated system that handles feeding, precision pill counting, labeling, real-time imprint monitoring, and automated removal of non-conforming units. The line operates under global digital control. Supporting processes include extraction, condensation, chromatography, crystallization, filtration, and drying, governed by Good Extracting Practice standards. Tasly holds more than 500 regulatory approvals worldwide.

Tasly serves the pharmaceutical and healthcare sectors, focusing on cardiovascular indications such as stable ischemic heart disease and chronic stable angina, and metabolic conditions like hyperlipidemia. Clinical programs include the ORESA and CAESA trials; Phase III data were presented at the American College of Cardiology meeting. Collaboration partners have included the Trade Winds ASEAN Mission and BioJapan, indicating a global commercial and research orientation.

The company differentiates itself through an end-to-end quality system spanning Good Manufacturing Practice, Good Agricultural Practice for raw-material cultivation, Good Extracting Practice, and Good Laboratory Practice. This integrated approach, combined with the proprietary automated line, aims to ensure batch-to-batch consistency and bridge traditional botanical knowledge with modern pharmaceutical validation.', certifications=ARRAY['Good Manufacturing Practice (GMP)','Good Agricultural Practice (GAP)','Good Extracting Practice (GEP)','Good Laboratory Practice (GLP)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Botanical drug development", "Automatic dripping pill manufacturing", "Automated packaging", "Extraction", "Condensation", "Chromatography", "Crystallization", "Filtration", "Drying", "Clinical trial management (Phase II, III)", "Regulatory approval support", "Quality control (GMP, GAP, GEP, GLP)"], "industries": ["Pharmaceutical", "Botanical medicine", "Healthcare", "Clinical research"], "materials": ["Botanical/herbal ingredients", "Medicinal plants", "Danshen (Salvia miltiorrhiza)", "Puer tea extract", "T89 (Dantonic) compound"], "equipment": ["Proprietary automatic dripping pill and packaging production line (patented design, global digital control, digital analysis of key process parameters, intensive web-based control, high-speed operation, precision pill counting, label attachment, real-time automatic online imprint monitoring, automated incompliant product detection and removal)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["World''s largest proprietary automatic dripping pill and packaging production line", "First herbal medicine-derived compound (T89/Dantonic) to complete FDA Phase III global trial", "500+ worldwide regulatory approvals", "Fully automated production from feeding to finished product collection", "Integrated quality systems: GMP, GAP, GEP, GLP"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2006, headquartered in Rockville, Maryland -> 