UPDATE companies SET description='TechNH, Inc. was founded in 1982 in a small corner of an old mill building in Nashua, New Hampshire. The company has since relocated to Merrimack, New Hampshire, where it operates as a custom plastic injection molder serving clients worldwide.

The company specializes in precision plastic injection molding, offering insert molding, over-molding, and in-house mold making and repair. Secondary services include pad printing, assembly, and packaging. TechNH also provides design for manufacturability, mold flow analysis, and IQ/OQ/PQ validation through an in-house regulatory team. Workforce tenure is notable: nearly 40% of employees have over five years of service, and 25% have exceeded a decade.

TechNH serves the medical, defense, alternative energy, water treatment, and industrial sectors. Customer testimonials reference clients in Massachusetts, New Hampshire, and Pennsylvania, including healthcare and industrial accounts. The company is ISO 13485:2016 certified by TUV, FDA registered (21 CFR 820), ITAR registered, and UL recognized.

A core differentiator is the company''s five-step tool transfer process, designed to protect supply continuity and confirm tool condition without production downtime. TechNH emphasizes in-house mold making and regulatory expertise, allowing it to maintain compliance with critical standards alongside customers. Long-tenured staff and a culture built on adaptability, integrity, enthusiasm, pride in work, and reliability underpin its approach.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','ITAR','FDA 21 CFR 820','UL Recognized']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Insert molding", "Over-molding", "In-house mold making", "Mold repair", "Design for manufacturability", "Mold flow analysis", "Pad printing", "Assembly", "Packaging", "Tool transfer", "Cleanroom molding", "IQ/OQ/PQ validation", "Regulatory compliance support", "Quality control", "Engineering design services"], "industries": ["Medical", "Defense", "Alternative Energy", "Water Treatment", "Industrial Applications"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Injection molding machines (16-780 ton capacity)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Five-step tool transfer process protecting supply continuity", "In-house mold making and repair capabilities", "In-house regulatory team for ISO 13485, ITAR, FDA, and UL compliance"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1982 in Nashua, NH -> /about", "Headquarters Merrimack, NH -> db", "Machines 16-780 tons, shot weight 0.5-128 oz -> /capabilities", "Insert molding, over-molding -> /capabilities", "In-house mold making and repair -> /capabilities", "Secondary services: pad printing, assembly, packaging -> /capabilities", "Design for manufacturability, mold flow analysis -> /capabilities", "IQ/OQ/PQ validation -> /capabilities", "In-house regulatory team -> /capabilities", "ISO 13485:2016 certified by TUV -> /, /capabilities", "FDA registered, 21 CFR 820 -> /", "ITAR registered -> /, /capabilities, db", "UL Recognized -> /", "Industries: medica