UPDATE companies SET description='Technotronix operates from Anaheim, California, where it was founded in 1981. The company has grown over more than four decades into a full-service printed circuit board manufacturer serving OEMs, startups, and enterprises across multiple sectors.

The company provides end-to-end PCB services including layout, fabrication, assembly (through-hole, surface-mount, and mixed technology), box build, cable and wire harness assembly, and metal fabrication. It works with rigid, flexible, and metal-core substrates and places components ranging from fine-pitch BGAs and QFPs down to 0201 packages. Production spans prototype runs through high-volume in-line manufacturing, supported by Mycronic 200 placement machines, Heller reflow systems, wave soldering, and a BGA rework station. Quality inspection uses CRX-100 X-ray, benchtop AOI, and manual checks.

Technotronix serves the automotive, electronics, telecommunications, medical, renewable energy, and defense industries. Its medical portfolio includes ECG recorders, bio-analytical instruments, dialysis equipment, and hearing aids. The company also supports electric vehicle prototyping and LED lighting projects, working with OEMs, startups, and larger enterprises that require scalable, cost-effective manufacturing.

The company emphasizes flexibility, offering no minimum order quantities, 24-hour prototype assembly turnaround, and both kitted and turnkey options. It holds ISO 9001:2015, AS9100 Rev. D, and ANAB ISO/IEC 17021 accreditations, and maintains a global vendor network to meet time-critical demands. Technotronix states that customer relations, integrity, and real-time quality inspection differentiate its service.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9100 Rev. D','ANAB ISO/IEC 17021 Accreditation','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB layout", "PCB fabrication (rigid, flexible, metal core)", "PCB assembly (through-hole, surface mount, mixed technology)", "PCB prototype", "PCB box build", "Electro-mechanical box build", "Cable and wire harness assembly", "Metal fabrication", "Material management", "Turnkey PCB assembly", "BGA placement and rework", "Fine-pitch component placement (0201, CSP, flip chip)", "X-ray inspection (CRX-100)", "Automated optical inspection (BX benchtop)", "Manual inspection", "Lead-free assembly", "Chemical-free material options", "Kitted assembly", "Turnkey assembly"], "industries": ["automotive", "electronics", "telecommunications", "medical", "renewable energy", "defense"], "materials": ["Rigid PCB substrates", "Flexible PCB substrates", "Metal core PCB substrates", "Lead-free solder", "Chemical-free materials"], "equipment": ["Mycronic 200", "Heller reflow soldering systems", "Wave solder machine", "BGA rework station AH-6810", "CRX-100 X-ray inspection", "BX benchtop AOI machines", "Mydata placement machines"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "24 hours for prototype PCB assembly", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No minimum PCB order requirements", "24-hour prototype PCB assembly turnaround", "ANAB accredited ISO/IEC 17021 management systems certification", "Global vendor network for time-critical requirements", "Real-time quality inspection with CRX-100 X-ray and benchtop AOI"], "facts_used": ["Fou