UPDATE companies SET description='Texas Instruments traces its roots to 1930 when Geophysical Service Inc., a small oil and gas exploration firm, opened in Dallas, Texas. The company pivoted during World War II, applying signal‑processing expertise to submarine detection and radar, and established an electronics equipment laboratory in 1946. In the 1950s it reorganized as Texas Instruments Inc., entering the semiconductor industry with the invention of the silicon transistor in 1954 and Jack Kilby’s breakthrough integrated circuit in 1958.

TI designs, manufactures, and sells analog and embedded processing semiconductors. Its portfolio exceeds 80,000 products, including analog ICs, embedded processors, and wireless transceivers. The company runs a global manufacturing network that includes 300 mm wafer fabs powered entirely by renewable electricity, producing tens of billions of chips annually. With roughly 33,000 employees worldwide, TI handles everything from process technology and design through packaging, test, and delivery.

The company serves more than 100,000 customers across automotive, industrial, consumer electronics, communications, data‑center, and medical‑equipment markets. Its chips power vehicle electrification and safety systems, factory automation, smartphones, optical networking gear, and life‑saving medical devices. TI emphasizes supply‑chain reliability, promising delivery “in any geopolitical environment.”

TI’s stated mission is to make electronics more affordable through semiconductors. It operates with three long‑term ambitions: act like owners who will own the company for decades, adapt to a changing world, and be a company its people are proud of. Differentiators cited include a 40,000‑patent portfolio, over $2 billion in annual R&D spending, and a comprehensive analog‑and‑embedded product breadth that lets engineers consolidate sourcing.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Analog IC design", "Embedded processor design", "Semiconductor wafer fabrication", "Assembly and packaging", "Test and reliability qualification", "Quality management (anti-counterfeit, product change notification, product life cycle)", "Environmental compliance (RoHS, lead-free)", "Automotive PPAP support", "Failure analysis", "Kilby Labs advanced research"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Industrial", "Consumer Electronics", "Communications", "Data Center", "Personal Electronics", "Medical Equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Tens of billions of chips per year", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["80,000+ analog and embedded processing products in portfolio", "Global manufacturing with 300\u202fmm wafer fabs using 100% renewable electricity", "40,000+ patents held worldwide", "$2B+ annual R&D investment", "Tens of billions of chips produced each year"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1930 as Geophysical Service Inc. -> /about", "Headquarters Dallas, Texas -> /about", "33,000+ employees -> /about", "80,000+ products -> /about", "Tens of billions chips/year -> /about", "100,000+ customers -> /about", "Automotive, Industrial, Consumer Electronics, Communications industries -> /about and /", "Data center, Personal electronics, Medical equipment -> / and /about", "300mm wafer fabs with 100% renewable electricity -> /", "40,000+ patents -> /", "$2B+ R&D investment -> /", "$370M TI Foundation giving since 1964 -> /", "$71M+ STEM education since 201