UPDATE companies SET description='The Plastics Group of America (TPG) is headquartered in Woonsocket, Rhode Island. The company traces its roots to 1973 when Bob Lebeaux founded Ralco Industries, Inc., a one-man operation buying and selling scrap plastics. In 1978 the firm added a grinder, baler, extruder and tractor‑trailer to enter recycling, and in 1980 began custom compounding reinforced thermoplastics under the Polifil® trade name. The business was renamed The Plastics Group of America in 1988, consolidating Ralco, Polifil® and the Transcontinental Polymers recycling unit. Today the company remains family‑led, with Lebeaux family members holding key executive and operational roles.

TPG operates more than 300,000 square feet of manufacturing space in Woonsocket, including the former Jules Desurmont Mill complex acquired in 2012. With a workforce of 60‑plus employees and annual revenue exceeding $50 million, the company custom‑compounds mineral‑ and glass‑filled polypropylene resins to precise mechanical, thermal and physical specifications. Its on‑site quality laboratory performs melt index, Izod, flexural, tensile, DSC, moisture, ash, Gardner impact and color testing on every batch. Beyond compounding, TPG provides recycling and toll‑processing services, color matching at no charge, and acts as a resin broker and distributor with stock ready for shipment.

The company serves processors in appliance, automotive, construction, consumer housewares, furniture, industrial/institutional/electronic, medical and personal care, packaging, and pump/pool/spa/irrigation markets. Customers include injection molders, extruders and blow‑molders who rely on TPG’s Polifil® resins for consistent performance in demanding applications.

TPG emphasizes its asset‑based manufacturing model, ISO 9001 certification and an on‑site testing lab as differentiators that enable tight lot‑to‑lot consistency whether the order is 100 pounds or one million pounds. The firm also highlights its recycling expertise, free color compounding, and a technical insights library that helps customers optimize molding processes.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','OSHA SHARP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom compounding of polypropylene resins", "Recycling and toll processing", "Color matching and compounding", "Resin distribution and brokerage", "Quality control testing (melt index, Izod, flexural, tensile, DSC, moisture, ash, Gardner impact, color)", "Technical consulting and processing guides", "Extrusion", "Grinding and baling", "Densifying and guillotining", "Gas injection molding assistance", "Sequential valve gating guidance", "Mold design troubleshooting", "Material property optimization"], "industries": ["Appliance", "Automotive", "Construction", "Consumer Housewares and Disposables", "Furniture", "Industrial/Institutional/Electronic", "Medical & Personal Care", "Packaging", "Pump/Pool/Spa/Irrigation"], "materials": ["Polypropylene", "Mineral-filled polypropylene", "Glass-filled polypropylene", "Talc", "Calcium carbonate", "Glass fiber", "Barium sulfate", "Scrap plastics"], "equipment": ["Grinders", "Balers", "Extruders", "Tractor-trailers", "On-line rheometers", "Transformers", "Solar panels", "Electrical control room"], "volume": "100 pounds to 1 million pounds", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["On-site testing lab with full physical property capabilities", "Free custom color compounding with lot-to-lot consistency", "Recycling and toll processing of customer scrap", "ISO 9001 certified quality system", "Over 300,000 sq ft of manufacturing capacity"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1973 by Bob Lebeaux as Ralco Industries -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Woonsocket, Rhode Island -> /about-us", "Family-owned with Lebeaux family in leadership -> /about-us", "Over 300,000 sq ft manufacturing space -> /", "60+ employees and over $50 million annual revenue -> /about-us", "ISO 9001 certified -> /about-us", "OSHA SHARP award 1997 -> /about-us", "Custom compounding of mineral and glass reinforced polypropylenes (Polifil\u00ae) -> /", "Recycling and toll processing services -> /services", "Color matching at no charge -> /services", "Distribution and brokerage of resins -> /services", "On-site testing lab with melt index, Izod, flexural, tensile, DSC, moisture, ash, Gardner impact, color testing -> /services", "Industries served: appliance, automotive, construction, consumer housewares, furniture, industrial/institutional/electronic, medical, packaging, pump/pool/spa/irrigation -> /about-us", "Equipment: grinders, balers, extruders, tractor-trailers, on-line rheometers, transformers, solar panels -> /about-us, /services", "Volume range: 100 pounds to 1 million pounds -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "we are primarily an asset-based manufacturer, capable of custom-compounding resins to the physical, mechanical, and thermal specifications your application requires", "founded_year": "1973", "employee_count": "60+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/6985369/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='the-plastics-group-of-america' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The Sheet Metal Shop operates from Columbus, Ohio, as a veteran- and family-owned fabrication business. The company does not disclose a founding year, but its principals describe decades of industry experience behind the operation.

The shop provides precision sheet metal fabrication across a range of processes: plasma cutting, welding (including artistic, industrial, architectural, and stainless steel), custom ductwork, exhaust systems, HVAC components, grease ducts, roof curbs, roof rails, security cages, and specialized fittings. Materials worked include stainless steel, aluminum, carbon steel, and black iron.

Customers span construction, manufacturing, and HVAC sectors, serving both residential and commercial clients throughout Columbus and Central Ohio. Projects range from custom HVAC sheet metal and duct fabrication to architectural metal art and anti-theft equipment enclosures.

