UPDATE companies SET description='The Wood Factory operates from Winterport, Maine, where it produces historically accurate millwork with a focus on Victorian-era gingerbread treatments.

The shop specializes in reproducing Victorian designs that have been researched from turn-of-the-century catalogues, photographs, and architectural drawings. In addition to its catalog of standard patterns, the company offers custom matching services, working from customer sketches, photographs, architects'' renderings, or original samples sent to the facility. Specific production processes, facility size, headcount, and annual volumes are not published.

Its customer base includes individuals seeking to restore or replicate Victorian gingerbread details, as well as design professionals who provide renderings or original samples for replication.

The company distinguishes itself through its research-driven approach to historical accuracy, drawing on primary sources from the Victorian era, and by offering custom replication services that accommodate a range of input formats, from hand-drawn sketches to physical samples.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Historical millwork production", "Victorian gingerbread treatments", "Historical design research", "Custom design matching", "Millwork replication from samples"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Historical restoration", "Architecture and design", "Millwork"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Historically accurate Victorian designs researched from turn-of-the-century catalogues, photographs, and architectural drawings", "Custom matching from customer sketches, photographs, architect renderings, and original samples", "Affordable pricing for historically accurate millwork"], "facts_used": ["Company name: The Wood Factory -> db", "Location: Winterport, Maine -> db", "Produces historically accurate millwork, Victorian gingerbread treatments -> /about-us", "Designs researched from turn-of-the-century catalogues, photographs, architectural drawings -> /about-us", "Custom matching from customer sketches, photographs, architect renderings, original samples -> /about-us", "Website: thewoodfactorymillwork.com -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "producing historically accurate millwork", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='the-wood-factory' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The Wooden Nickel operates from Arab, Alabama, where it builds custom live‑edge furniture from locally sourced hardwood slabs. The company does not publish a founding year or ownership structure, but its blog posts describe a shop that began with a focus on honest craftsmanship — turning rough logs into dining tables, desks, and workstations meant to last generations.

Production centers on kiln‑dried slabs sourced from tree services and loggers. Each piece moves through stabilization, flattening, sanding, and, when needed, resin filling of cracks or knots before receiving multiple hand‑applied finish coats. Steel bases — ranging from simple dark‑finished legs to adjustable‑height desk frames made from high‑tolerance steel — are fitted in‑house. The shop handles one‑off commissions and larger custom runs alike, though it does not disclose facility size, headcount, or annual volume.

Customers span residential and commercial segments. A Marshall County family commissioned a three‑generation dining table; remote workers order wide slab workstations with cable management; local businesses have requested reinforced tables for offices, break rooms, and public areas that endure daily wear. The company notes that the same durability valued by commercial clients appeals to homeowners as well.

The Wooden Nickel positions itself against mass‑produced furniture, emphasizing “no templates, no shortcuts” and a slow, deliberate process — “if it wouldn’t hold up in our own homes, it doesn’t leave the shop.” The stated goal is furniture built for real life: sturdy, honest, and meant to outlast a warranty card.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Live edge furniture manufacturing", "Custom furniture design", "Kiln drying and stabilization", "Slab flattening and sanding", "Resin crack and knot filling", "Multi-layer hand finishing", "Steel base fabrication", "Adjustable desk frame assembly", "Commercial contract furniture construction"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Commercial furniture", "Contract furniture", "Home office furniture"], "materials": ["Kiln-dried hardwood slabs", "Steel (bases and adjustable frames)", "Epoxy resin", "Wood finishes"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Custom orders from single pieces to large volumes", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom orders from single pieces to large volumes", "Locally sourced hardwood slabs from tree services and loggers", "No templates or shortcuts; each slab yields a one\u2011of\u2011a\u2011kind piece", "In\u2011house steel base fabrication including adjustable desk frames with high\u2011tolerance steel", "Multi\u2011layer hand\u2011applied finish; pieces inspected to household\u2011use standard"], "facts_used": ["Location: Arab, Alabama -> db", "Website: thewoodennickel.net -> db", "Custom live edge furniture (dining tables, desks, workstations) -> pages:/", "Kiln-dried hardwood slabs sourced from tree services and loggers -> pages:/", "Processes: stabilization, flattening, sanding, resin work, multi-layer finishing -> pages:/", "Steel bases and adjustable desk frames with high-tolerance steel -> pages:/", "Custom orders from single items to large volumes -> pages:/", "Residential customers (families, home offices) -> pages:/", "Commercial customers (local businesses, offices, break rooms, public spaces) -> pages:/", "Differentiators: no templates, no shortcuts, household durability standard -> pages:/"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Most of our production is custom orders. We can produce single items, or large custom orders.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='the-wooden-nickel-custom-live-edge-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The Thos. Moser Freeport Showroom occupies a restored nineteenth-century home in Freeport, Maine, two blocks north of L.L.Bean’s flagship store. The company has not disclosed a founding date for this location, its ownership structure, or the names of its founders. The showroom is managed by Steve Wyman, who also heads the Customer in Residence (CIR) program.

The showroom presents two floors of Thos. Moser furniture designs alongside Maine artwork, with an attached carriage house serving as an outlet annex offering immediately available pieces. The facility provides scheduled consultations for both standard and custom furniture designs through the CIR program. Operating hours run Monday through Saturday 10 a.m. to 5 p.m. and Sunday noon to 5 p.m., with holiday closures observed. The showroom also hosts events such as the “On Display: Dedicated to Art” exhibition, which pairs paintings and prints with handmade wooden furniture through October 31, 2026.

The showroom serves visitors to Maine, including residential customers and design professionals seeking Thos. Moser furniture. A “Commercial Products” link on the company’s website suggests outreach to commercial clients, though specific industries are not detailed. The showroom’s primary role is to display and sell the manufacturer’s furniture rather than to produce it.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Customer service", "Design consultations", "Custom furniture design assistance", "Customer in Residence program"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Restored 19th-century home showcasing two floors of furniture and Maine artwork", "Carriage house outlet annex with immediately available designs", "Customer in Residence program providing scheduled design consultations", "Flagship showroom location two blocks from L.L.Bean\u2019s flagship store"], "facts_used": ["Location: Freeport, Maine, 149 Main Street -> /", "Restored nineteenth-century home with two floors of furniture and artwork -> /", "Carriage house outlet annex with immediately available designs -> /", "Manager Steve Wyman heads Customer in Residence program -> /", "Operating hours Monday-Saturday 10am-5pm, Sunday 12pm-5pm -> /", "Events such as ''On Display: Dedicated to Art'' exhibition -> /", "Commercial Products link on website -> /", "Showroom does not manufacture furniture -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "our flagship showroom is a convenient and picturesque stop if you visit Maine. We restored a nineteenth-century home and furnished two full floors with classic and new Thos. Moser furniture designs and Maine artwork. An attached carriage house serves as our outlet annex", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=no