UPDATE companies SET description='Throttle Down Kustoms operates from Moore, Montana, where it was established in April 2004 after owner Jeremy Pulse purchased his former employer, Advance Frame Works, and renamed the business. Pulse, a graduate of WyoTech’s Auto Body Technology and Chassis Fabrication program, began building custom truck bumpers in his spare time in the early 2000s before transitioning to full‑time fabrication when demand outgrew his side project.

The company designs, engineers, and builds rugged steel front and rear bumpers for Chevrolet Silverado, Dodge RAM, Ford F‑Series, and GMC Sierra trucks, as well as steel Jeep frames, skid plates, and lightweight aluminum dog boxes for trucks, ATVs, and UTVs. Production relies on CNC laser cutting of 3/16‑inch and 1/4‑inch PNO solid steel plate, CNC mandrel bending of 2"x4" rectangular A500 tubing, and hand welding performed by certified fabricators who have completed recognized chassis‑fabrication programs. All work is carried out in‑house at the Moore facility.

Products serve individual truck owners — ranch hands, off‑road enthusiasts, and commercial users — along with custom‑fabrication clients needing enclosed trailers, rock‑crawling buggies, street rods, and diesel‑powered truggies. The company ships worldwide, with a typical lead time of 8 to 12 weeks for fabricated items.

Throttle Down Kustoms emphasizes domestic manufacturing, a lifetime warranty on every product, and mandrel‑bent frames that are described as sturdier and more precise than welded alternatives. The founder’s commitment to hiring only certified, formally trained fabricators and using U.S.‑sourced steel is presented as the core differentiator.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Auto Body Technology and Chassis Fabrication", "Custom fabrication", "CNC laser cutting", "CNC mandrel bending", "Hand welding", "Design and engineering", "Frame construction", "Bumper fabrication", "Skid plate fabrication", "Jeep frame fabrication", "Aluminum dog box fabrication"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Off\u2011road equipment", "Recreational vehicles", "Custom metal fabrication"], "materials": ["PNO solid steel plate (3/16\" and 1/4\")", "A500 tubing (2\"x4\" rectangular wall)", "Aluminum", "Grade 8 hardware"], "equipment": ["CNC laser cutter", "CNC mandrel bender"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "8 to 12 weeks", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All products made in USA (Moore, Montana)", "Lifetime warranty on every item", "Mandrel\u2011bent frames instead of welded frames", "Certified fabricators from accredited chassis programs", "Custom fabrication capability beyond standard bumpers"], "facts_used": ["Location: Moore, Montana -> db, /, /about", "Founded April 2004, Jeremy Pulse bought Advance Frame Works -> /about", "Founder Jeremy Pulse, WyoTech degree in Auto Body Technology and Chassis Fabrication -> /about", "Products: steel bumpers for Chevy, Dodge, Ford, GMC; Jeep frames, skid plates, aluminum dog boxes -> /, /about", "Processes: CNC laser cut PNO steel plate, CNC mandrel bent A500 tubing, hand welding by certified professionals -> /, /about, products", "Custom fabrications: enclosed trailers, rock crawling buggies, street rods, diesel truggies -> /about", "Mandrel bent frames, avoid welded frames -> /about", "Lifetime warranty on all products -> /, /about", "Lead time 8 to 12 weeks -> products", "Materials: 3/16\" and 1/4\" PNO steel plate, A500 tubing, aluminum, Grade 8 hardware -> products, /about", "Equipment: CNC laser cutter, CNC mandrel bender -> products, /about", "Industries served: automotive aftermarket, off-road, recreational, custom fabrication -> /, /about", "Company type: Manufacturer (design, engineer, construct) -> /, /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We design, engineer, and construct rugged steel front bumpers and rear bumpers for Chevy Silverado, Dodge RAM, Ford F-Series, and GMC Sierra trucks. We also make steel Jeep frames and skid plates. Everything we make is made from CNC laser cut PNO solid steel plate, and hand welded by certified professionals in Moore, Montana, USA.", "founded_year": "2004", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='throttle-down-kustoms-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Thunderbird Molding operates from Elkhart, Indiana, with additional facilities in Shelbyville, Illinois, and Greensboro. The company is Thunderbird-owned and actively managed, though a founding year and founder names are not publicly disclosed. It began as a resource for high-precision custom plastic injection molding and contract manufacturing.

The shop runs injection molding presses up to 1,500 tons and maintains an inventory of more than 800 molds, supported by a quick-mold-change system and proprietary batch molding procedures. Services span mold design, prototyping, engineering, production, and assembly, including insert molding, over molding (press-to-press transfer), finishing, and secondary operations. A 3D printing cell using carbon printing technology provides an alternative for low-volume end-use parts with properties comparable to injection molding. The company states it holds repeatable tolerances to ±0.0002 in.

Customers come from medical device, automotive, defense, drinkware, and lighting sectors. The firm highlights lens-grade molding for critical defense components and contaminant-free polymers for optical applications. It serves OEMs needing prototype-to-production support, short-run and low-volume orders, and scalable production into the millions.

Thunderbird Molding emphasizes a “performance under pressure” philosophy, citing a 2.5-second cycle time on an 8-cavity mold and a 99% success rate reworking close-tolerance molds to compensate for shrinkage and warpage. Certifications include ISO 9001:2015, ITAR registration, PPAP and SPI compliance, and UL QMMY2 certification.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ITAR registered','PPAP compliant','SPI compliant','UL QMMY2 certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom plastic injection molding", "Insert molding", "Over molding (press-to-press transfer)", "Finishing and secondary services", "Injection molding tool transfer", "Mold design", "Prototyping", "Engineering support", "Production molding", "Assembly services", "Short-run / low-volume production", "Prototype-to-production support", "3D printing (carbon printing) for end-use parts", "Quick-mold-change system", "Proprietary batch molding procedures", "Just-in-time delivery", "Lens-grade molding (reduced weld lines)", "Automated 3D video inspection", "Tensile/flexural raw material testing", "PPAP and SPI compliance", "Digital project and production tracking"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Automotive", "Defense", "Drinkware", "Lighting"], "materials": ["Lens-quality polymers (contaminant-free)"], "equipment": ["Injection molding presses up to 1,500 tons", "Multi-sensor metrology systems", "Automated 3D video inspection systems", "High-end moisture analyzers", "Digital height gauges", "Gauge pins", "Torque scales", "Micrometers", "Spectrophotometer", "3D printers (carbon printing)"], "volume": "Prototype to millions of units; short-run and low-volume production", "lead_time": "Just-in-time delivery for short runs", "tolerances": "\u00b10.0002 in", "built_on": ["Presses up to 1,500 tons with redundant capacity for millions of parts", "800+ mold inventory with quick-mold-change and proprietary batch molding", "Repeatable tolerances to \u00b10.0002 in", "ISO 9001:2015, ITAR, PPAP, SPI, UL QMMY2 certified", "3D printing (carbon) for low-volume end-use parts"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters Elkhart, Indiana -> db", "Additional facilities Shelbyville, Illinois; Greensboro -> /", "Thunderbird-owned and actively managed -> /quality", "Presses up to 1,500 tons -> /", "800+ mold inventory -> /", "Quick-mold-change system -> /", "Proprietary batch molding procedures -> /", "Insert molding and over molding -> /", "Finishing and secondary services -> /", "Injection molding tool transfer -> /", "Mold design, prototyping, engineering, production, assembly -> /", "3D printing (carbon) for low-volume end-use parts -> /, /products", "Repeatable tolerances \u00b10.0002 in -> /quality", "ISO 9001:2015 registered -> /quality", "ITAR registered -> /quality", "PPAP and SPI compliant -> /quality", "UL QMMY2 certified -> /quality", "Medical device industry -> /industries_served, /", "Automotive industry -> /", "Defense industry (lens-grade parts) -> /", "Drinkware and lighting -> /", "2.5-second cycle time on 8-cavity mold -> /quality", "99% success rate reworking close-tolerance molds -> /quality", "Automated 3D video inspection -> /quality", "Tensile/flexural raw material testing -> /quality", "Multi-sensor metrology systems -> /quality", "High-end moisture analyzers -> /quality", "Digital height gauges, gauge pins, torque scales, micrometers -> /quality", "Spectrophotometer -> /quality", "Digital project and production tracking -> /quality", "Just-in-time delivery for short runs -> /", "Lens-quality polymers contaminant-free -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "An experienced resource for high-precision custom plastic injection molding and contract manufacturing, we offer comprehensive mold design, prototyping, engineering, production, and assembly services.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='thunderbird-molding-elkhart' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Tillet Custom Fabrication operates from Middleton, Wisconsin, serving the greater Madison area. The business is a sole proprietorship run by Gabriel, who presents himself as the primary fabricator and point of contact. No founding year is published on the site.

The shop delivers custom metal fabrication across a wide range of processes: welding (including cast iron and exotic metals), CNC plasma cutting, machining, tube bending, and vacuum‑insulated pipe work for cryogenic liquids. Projects span marine repairs such as pontoon and skeg work, automotive builds like exhausts, manifolds, roll cages and turbo kits, custom railings (ADA‑compliant), furniture, outdoor fixtures, solar panel frames and mounts, beavertail boat pods, trailer repairs and winch mounts. The operation appears to be a small, hands‑on facility; no square‑footage or headcount figures are disclosed.

Customers come from marine, automotive, residential and aerospace sectors. The site lists concrete examples: pontoon railings, custom exhaust systems, stair and ramp railings, tables and benches, bistro light fixtures, cryogenic piping, and aerospace‑grade fabrication.

Gabriel emphasizes transparent, upfront pricing with no hidden costs and pledges constant communication until a job is complete. Free quotes are offered on every inquiry.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom metal fabrication", "Marine repairs (pontoon, railings, skeg/lower unit)", "Automotive fabrication (exhausts, tubing, manifolds, brackets, roll cages, turbo kits, down pipes, charge pipes, blow off valves, waste gates)", "Custom railing (indoor/outdoor, ADA compliant grab bars)", "Custom furniture (tables, benches)", "Outdoor projects (bistro light fixtures, mailboxes, address signs)", "Rust repair", "Cast iron welding", "Vacuum insulated pipe for cryogenic liquids", "Tube bending", "Aerospace fabrication", "CNC plasma cutting", "Machining", "Solar panel frames and mounts", "Beavertail boat pods", "Trailer repairs", "Winch mounts"], "industries": ["Marine", "Automotive", "Residential", "Aerospace"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Stainless steel", "Exotic metals"], "equipment": ["CNC plasma cutter"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Transparent, upfront estimates with no hidden fees", "Constant communication throughout the project", "Free quotes on all inquiries"], "facts_used": ["Middleton, Wisconsin location -> /", "Sole proprietor Gabriel -> /", "Custom metal fabrication services -> /", "Materials: aluminum, stainless steel, exotic metals -> /", "Industries: marine, auto, residential, aerospace -> /", "Services list including marine repairs, auto, railing, furniture, etc. -> /", "Transparent pricing, upfront estimates -> /", "Constant communication until job done -> /", "Free quotes -> /", "CNC plasma cutting -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "I am skilled in a wide range of metal fabrication and machining.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tillet-custom-fabrication' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
